            <ArticleTitle>An Unusual Foreign Body in the Heart: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5761/atcs.cr.17-00117</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Penetrating foreign bodies in the heart is rare and may lead to life-threatening complications. Early diagnosis and removal are crucial for these rare cases. We report a case of accidental penetrating sewing needle in the right ventricle. The needle was successfully removed without open heart surgery and cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB), after accurate localization using transthoracic echocardiography (TTE).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
